From 61db38c15e3ee86e41f5d962b061abd949fc5153 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 01:31:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Capture replaces the screenshot panel

Capture is Luma's screenshot and screen recording tool, drawn in the
shelf's surface language instead of GNOME's OSD panel.

- One bar, SHELF_SURFACE_GAP beyond the dock island's desktop-facing edge
  (placeShelfBar in lumaShelfSurface.js; SHELF_INSET above the work area
  with the dock at a side), with Close, three screenshot modes (entire
  screen, a window, a selection), two recording modes, Options and a
  labelled Capture or Record button. Quick Options' tokens in light, dark,
  frost and glass. Tooltips, the Options menu, the recording pill and the
  thumbnail are placed from the bar by the same rule.
- Nothing is selected when Capture opens. Dragging draws a selection;
  choosing a selection mode draws the last one (Remember Last Selection)
  or a box 42% of the monitor wide and tall, 18% from its top. A dashed
  outline, eight handles, the size in physical pixels, a 24 by 24 minimum,
  and a double click takes it.
- Windows stay where they are; the one under the pointer gets an accent
  outline over an accent wash and a click takes it. The monitor under the
  pointer is outlined and a click anywhere takes it.
- Ctrl+Shift+2 (screenshot-window) opens window mode waiting for a pick
  instead of capturing the focused window. Ctrl+Shift+1 opens the mode last
  used, Ctrl+Shift+3 selection, Ctrl+Shift+4 recording or stops one.
- Options: Save to Pictures (Screenshots), Videos (Screencasts) for
  recordings, Desktop, Clipboard for screenshots, or a folder chosen
  through the portal's file chooser; a 5 or 10 second timer counting down
  over the live screen, Escape cancelling it; Show Floating Thumbnail,
  Remember Last Selection, Show Pointer. All kept in
  org.project_luma.capture. Messages and Record Sound are not offered: the
  recorder captures video only.
- "Screenshot YYYY-MM-DD at HH.MM.SS.png" and "Recording YYYY-MM-DD at
  HH.MM.SS.webm". A floating thumbnail beside the shelf opens the file and
  replaces the screenshot and screencast notifications; failures still
  notify. The result is announced to screen readers.
- A recording shows a pill with a pulsing dot, the time and Stop where the
  bar was; Stop, Ctrl+Shift+4 or Escape end it. GNOME's screen recording
  indicator is not shown.
- The pill, a recording's outline, the countdown, the flash and the
  thumbnail paint only into the stage views, so they are never in a
  screenshot or recording.
- Opening from Luma's search keeps the search out of the capture.

Dropping this patch restores GNOME's screenshot UI.
